cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Computational Analysis of Spanish-English Code-switching"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-24"
authors:
  - family-names: "Shi"
    given-names: "Meiyun"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible Python pipeline for conservative within-utterance
  Spanish-English code-switching analysis in the Bangor Miami Corpus. The
  software parses CHAT headers, aligns pseudonymised speakers with questionnaire
  metadata without guessing unresolved identities, reads heterogeneous
  word-level TSV files, identifies transitions from corpus-provided language
  annotations, calculates participant-level switching rates, and performs
  descriptive and inferential statistical analysis.
keywords:
  - code-switching
  - computational linguistics
  - corpus linguistics
  - bilingualism
  - natural language processing
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/shimeiyun/bangor-miami-code-switching"
url: "https://github.com/shimeiyun/bangor-miami-code-switching"
